# SA Bank - Software Requirements Specification (SRS)

## 1. Introduction
SA Bank is a banking management system designed to provide basic banking services through a simple and secure system.

## 2. Purpose
The purpose of this system is to manage customer accounts and provide banking services efficiently.

## 3. Scope
The system supports customer registration, login, account management, balance checking, money transfer, transaction history and bank administration.

## 4. Functional Requirements
- Customer Registration
- Customer Login
- Account Management
- Check Account Balance
- Money Transfer
- Transaction History
- Bank Admin Management

## 5. Non-Functional Requirements
- Security
- Reliability
- Easy to use
- Fast response
- Data accuracy

## 6. User Roles
### Customer
Customers can register, login, manage accounts, check balance, transfer money and view transaction history.

### Bank Admin
The administrator can manage customer accounts and banking information.

## 7. System Requirements
- Computer or laptop
- Internet connection
- Web browser
- GitHub repository

## 8. Conclusion
The SA Bank system provides a simple and organized solution for managing basic banking operations securely and efficiently.
